  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Purpose</h3>
  <p>
    The purpose of this policy is to provide guidelines to the administration, faculty and staff for student admission to the BSN program in the Department of Nursing.
  </p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Plan</h3>
  <p>
    Admission to the nursing program is selective. Nursing is a practice discipline which bears great responsibility for maintaining high ethical and intellectual standards. The admission process provides a method of selection that assures qualified applicants are granted admission.
  </p>

  <h4 style="margin-top: 20px;">Admission to the BSN program is a three-step process: The three-steps are:</h4>
  <ol>
    <li>Application and admission to Heritage University.</li>
    <li>Placement in the pre-nursing pathway.</li>
    <li>Application and acceptance to the BSN program.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Policies and Procedures</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Policy:</strong> Individuals seeking admission to the BSN program offered by Heritage University Department of Nursing must meet the admission criteria of Heritage University prior to consideration for admission to the nursing program. Prospective students apply to Heritage University indicating desire for admission to the pre-nursing pathway. Once it has been determined that an individual has met Heritage University's admission standards, the student may pursue pre-nursing pathway (Nursing Policy #{{ nursing_policy_number }}) or apply for early admission to the BSN program (qualifications below). Neither admission to Heritage University, nor placement in the pre-nursing pathway guarantees admission to the BSN program. Admission to the BSN program is selective. The criteria for admission are described in the procedures below.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Procedure:</strong> The procedure, adopted for use by the Administration, Progression, Retention, and Graduation Committee, is designed to reduce bias in the selection process.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Step 1:</strong> Meet admission requirements to Heritage University as designated by the Heritage University catalog <a href="{{ catalog_url }}">http://catalog.heritage.edu/</a>.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">Step 2: Admission to the pre-Nursing Pathway or Early Admission</h2>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 20px;">A. Requirements for a HIGH SCHOOL SENIOR to be considered for Pre-Nursing Pathway</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>High school 3.00 GPA on a 4-point scale.</li>
    <li>Successful completion of these high school courses: English (4 units); college-prep mathematics (3 units); social sciences (2 units); biology and chemistry (2 units).</li>
    <li>Each course is to be completed with a grade of 2.00 (C) or better.</li>
    <li>Completed application and admission to Heritage University.</li>
    <li>Compass score consistent with placement into college level MATH 140 and ENG 101 upon admission to Heritage University.</li>
    <li>Eligibility for placement in CHEM 101, CHEM 105 or CHEM 110 per evaluation by Heritage University Chemistry professor.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 20px;">B. Requirements for a HIGH SCHOOL SENIOR or CURRENT 1st-YEAR of COLLEGE HERITAGE STUDENT to be considered for Early Admission to the BSN Program:</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>High school 3.00 GPA on a 4-point scale.</li>
    <li>Successful completion of these high school courses:
      <ul>
        <li>English (4 units)</li>
        <li>college-prep mathematics (4 units) including pre-calculus, calculus, and/or statistics (3 units)</li>
        <li>social science (2 units)</li>
        <li>science (3 units): biology (1 unit), chemistry (1 unit); additional chemistry, biology, physics, and related sciences (1 unit).</li>
      </ul>
      Each course is to be completed with a grade of 3.00 (B) or better.
    </li>
    <li>Composite ACT score of 26 or better or SAT score of 1230 or better.</li>
    <li>Compass score consistent with placement into college level MATH 140 and ENG 101 upon admission to Heritage University.</li>
    <li>Completed application and admission to Heritage University.</li>
    <li>Development and adherence to an individualized academic plan to efficiently complete all BSN program prerequisites.</li>
    <li>Complete "Step 3" below the year prior to the "Sophomore Year" in the BSN Program.</li>
    <li>Once admitted to the BSN program, the student must achieve a "B-" or better in all NUR courses and other courses required for the BSN degree. [see progression policy]</li>
    <li>If the student attains and maintains the above requirements, the Chair of APRG may approve early admission to the BSN program but does not mean all of the above requirements, the student will be placed in the "Pre-Nursing Pathway."</li>
  </ol>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 20px;">C. Requirements for a CURRENT HERITAGE STUDENT requesting major change to Pre-Nursing Pathway</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Overall minimum college GPA of 2.75 on a 4-point scale.</li>
    <li>Completion of at least one of the following: BIOL 110, CHEM 101, MATH 140.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 20px;">D. Requirements for a TRANSFER APPLICANT to be considered for Pre-Nursing Pathway</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Overall minimum college grade point average of 2.75 on a 4-point scale.</li>
    <li>Completed application and admission to Heritage University.</li>
    <li>Official copies of high school transcripts if fewer than 30 credits of college work completed.</li>
    <li>Official copies of all college transcripts.</li>
    <li>Completion of the equivalent of at least one of the following: BIOL 111, CHEM 101, MATH 140.</li>
    <li>Grade of C+ or better will be required in CHEM 101 and MATH 140.</li>
    <li>Completion of the equivalent of at least two of the following with a grade of at least C+ or better: PSY 101, SOC 101, PHIL 210, ENG 101 or UNIV 101.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 20px;">PREREQUISITE COURSEWORK</h3>
